        summary: "{D} stood by a school fence on {DATE} after being warned off. Dismissal was at 3 p.m., and the warning came ten minutes later. {D} stood by the fence near the pickup line.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "School Camera", "{D} stands by the fence."), E(.document, 2, "Pickup List", "{D} is not on the school's pickup list.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Waiting", "{DL} says {D.he} was waiting for a niece.")],
        role: "Principal",
        exam: [.direct("Why was {D} warned off?", "\"{D} was standing by the school fence near the pickup line after dismissal at 3 p.m., and {D.he} is not on our pickup list.\""), .direct("When did the warning come?", "\"About ten minutes after dismissal. I asked {D.him} to move away from the fence.\""), .direct("What does the camera show?", "\"It shows {DL} standing by the fence, watching the line. {DL} stayed there after the warning.\""), .direct("What are your pickup procedures at dismissal?", "\"Parents and approved adults wait in a car line or at the front gate and show a card. Our office keeps a list of who may take each child, and staff check it at the curb.\""), .direct("What did you notice about the defendant?", "\"{D.He} stood by the north fence, close to where the line starts, for about ten minutes with eyes on the children. {D.He} was not in the car line and did not have a card.\""), .direct("What did you say when you approached?", "\"I introduced myself and asked who {DL} was waiting for. {DL} named a niece, but could not give a teacher's name, and I asked {DL} to step away from the fence.\""), .cross("Did the defendant threaten anyone?", "\"No. {DL} did not speak to children and did not threaten anyone.\""), .cross("{D} has a niece enrolled at the school, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"I have learned that. A niece is enrolled, but {D.he} is not an approved pickup.\""), .cross("Did the defendant try to enter the school?", "\"No. {D.He} stayed outside the fence.\""), .cross("The niece is enrolled at your school, is that right?", "\"Yes, I have confirmed that since. {D.He} is not on the pickup list for that child, but the family is known to us.\""), .cross("{D} never spoke to any child or tried to enter, did {D.he}?", "\"That is right. {D.He} stayed outside the fence and did not approach a student, and I was not aware of any contact.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} loitered at a school.", "A waiting uncle."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} is not on the pickup list.", "The niece is enrolled."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why were you standing at the school fence?", "\"I was waiting for my niece. I wanted to see {V.him} come out and say hello after school.\""), .direct("Are you on the school's pickup list?", "\"No, I am not. I was just waiting to say hello, and I did not know that mattered.\""), .direct("How long had you been standing there?", "\"About ten minutes. I was not hiding, and I did not speak to any child or try to go inside.\""), .direct("How did you know when your niece would come out?", "\"My sibling texted that morning asking me to meet the child at dismissal because of a work conflict. I got there about two minutes before the bell.\""), .direct("What did you think about the list?", "\"I did not know there was one. My sibling said to just wait at the fence, and that is what I did.\""), .direct("What did you do after you were told to move?", "\"I stepped back about ten feet but stayed on the sidewalk, because I did not want my niece to come out and not see me. Then deputies were called.\""), .cross("You were warned and you stayed, didn't you?", "\"I did. I did not understand what the problem was, and I thought I would be gone soon.\""), .cross("You are not on the list. Why wait right there?", "\"I wanted to see my niece. I did not think it was wrong to stand outside a public fence.\""), .cross("The principal asked you to move away, didn't the principal?", "\"Someone asked me. I did not realize how serious it was until deputies came.\""), .cross("You were told to leave and you stayed, correct?", "\"I moved back but I did not leave, and I can see now why that looked bad. I thought explaining who I was would be enough.\""), .cross("You could have called the school or your sibling right then, couldn't you?", "\"Yes. I should have phoned the office, and I did not think of it until the deputy asked me.\"")],
        openings: ("After dismissal at 3 p.m., {D} stood by an elementary school fence near the pickup line. Ten minutes later the principal warned {D} off, and {D} stayed, though {D} was not on the school's pickup list.", "The defense will present a relative who was asked by a sibling to meet a niece enrolled at the school. {D} spoke to no child, entered nothing, and had no idea a list existed."),
        closings: ("A school fence, a pickup line, a warning, and {D} still standing there. {D} is not on the pickup list, and schools set those rules to protect children.", "A relative waiting for a niece, with no contact with any child. The State must prove {D} meant to stay after an unlawful warning, and the niece's enrollment makes {D}'s story credible."),
        timeline: [(0, "3 p.m.: dismissal."), (0, "3:10 p.m.: the warning.")],
        identified: "School Camera",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let checkoutShove = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.checkoutShove",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Shopper Shoves Man in Checkout Line Over Cut"],
        law: "simpleAssault",
        spec: "Assaulted {V} by pushing {V.him}, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} shoved a shopper on {DATE} in a checkout line after {V.he} stepped ahead. The register had a single open lane, and the line ran back toward the aisle. The line formed at about 6 p.m., and the shove came three minutes later.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Store Camera", "{D} pushes {V}."), E(.statement, 2, "Cashier", "Saw {D} shove {V} in the line.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Cut", "{DL} says {V} cut the line.")],
        role: "Cashier",
        exam: [.direct("What did you see at your register at about 6 p.m. on {DATE}?", "\"We had a single open lane and a line that ran back toward the aisle. Three minutes after the line formed, there was a shove.\""), .direct("Who shoved whom?", "\"I saw {D} shove {V} in the line. {V} had stepped forward in front of {DL}, and then {DL} pushed.\""), .direct("What does the store camera show?", "\"It shows {DL} pushing {V}. You can see the line, the two of them, and the push.\""), .direct("What was the store like at 6 p.m.?", "\"It was the after-work rush, with only one register open and the line backing into the cereal aisle. People were holding full carts and getting restless.\""), .direct("What did you hear before the shove?", "\"I heard a raised voice, something like, the line starts back there. I looked up and saw {DL} stepping toward {V} at the front.\""), .direct("What happened right after?", "\"{D.He} put both hands on {V}'s shoulders and shoved. {V} stumbled into the candy rack and dropped a hand basket.\""), .cross("{DL} says {V} cut the line, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"I can't say whether {V} had been in line earlier. I only saw {V} step forward.\""), .cross("Was {V} hurt?", "\"{V} stumbled and was surprised. I don't recall any injury. It was a push, and {V} stayed on {V.his} feet.\""), .cross("Did {DL} say anything before the push?", "\"I heard some words, but I couldn't make out what they were. It was busy, and I was at the register.\""), .cross("{V} had a hand basket, correct?", "\"Yes, a small basket with a few items. {V} may have been holding a spot rather than cutting, though I could not see where {V} came from.\""), .cross("You were scanning items and watching at the same time, weren't you?", "\"Mostly scanning. I looked up when the voices rose, so I did not see the start of it.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} shoved a shopper.", "A line cut."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{V} had a hand basket.", "{V} was in line already."),
        defendant: [.direct("What happened in line?", "\"I was waiting. {V} stepped ahead of me and cut in. I told {V.him} to get back, and {V.he} didn't.\""), .direct("Why did you shove {V}?", "\"I was frustrated. I'd been waiting a while, and I pushed {V.him} to move {V.him} back. Injuring {V.him} was never my aim, but the push was my doing.\""), .direct("How do you feel about it?", "\"Honestly, I feel stupid. It was a small thing. I should have said something to the cashier instead.\""), .direct("How long had you been waiting?", "\"About fifteen minutes. I had a full cart and had moved up inch by inch, with a toddler fussing in the seat.\""), .direct("What did {V} do?", "\"{V} walked up from the side and stepped right in front of my cart, setting a basket down. I said that is not how it works, and {V} said I was already behind.\""), .direct("What were you thinking when you pushed?", "\"Nothing, really. I was tired and irritated, and the push happened before I thought about it.\""), .cross("You pushed {V}, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. The camera shows it.\""), .cross("Only one lane was open, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. People were irritated. That's no excuse, and I know it.\""), .cross("You could have called the cashier, couldn't you?", "\"I could have. I wasn't thinking. I reacted, and it's embarrassing.\""), .cross("You put both hands on {V}, didn't you?", "\"I did. I know it looks bad, and I wish I had called the cashier instead.\""), .cross("{V} stumbled into a rack because of you, correct?", "\"Yes, and I apologized right away. I should have said it before I used my hands.\"")],
        openings: ("In a checkout line with a single open lane at 6 p.m., {D} shoved {V} three minutes after the line formed. The store camera and the cashier both saw it, and {V} stumbled into a rack.", "Jurors will see a person who says {V} cut the line, who had waited fifteen minutes with a child in the cart, and who reacted once out of frustration. No one was hurt."),
        closings: ("A long line, an argument, and two hands on {V}'s shoulders, all on camera. Frustration with a line never gives anyone the right to shove a stranger.", "{D} reacted once, in a tired moment, to someone who stepped in ahead of a long wait. The State has not proved more than a regretted push that hurt no one."),
        timeline: [(0, "6 p.m.: the line."), (0, "6:03 p.m.: the shove.")],
        identified: "Store Camera",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["V": .male])

    static let roadCones = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.roadCones",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Man Takes Work-Zone Cones for His Yard"],
        law: "misdLarceny",
        spec: "Stole property of {V}, a contractor, valued at $280, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} loaded fourteen traffic cones into a truck on {DATE}. The cones were stacked at dusk and were gone by 8 p.m. They were worth $280.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Work Zone Camera", "{D} loads cones."), E(.document, 2, "Equipment List", "Fourteen cones on the contractor's list.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Trash", "{DL} says they were discarded.")],
        role: "Site foreman",
        exam: [.direct("What happened to the cones?", "\"Fourteen traffic cones were stacked at dusk, and by 8 p.m. they were gone. They are worth about $280.\""), .direct("What does the work zone camera show?", "\"It shows {D} loading the cones into a truck. It is clear.\""), .direct("Are those cones on your equipment list?", "\"Yes. Fourteen cones are on the contractor's list, and they carry a company stamp.\""), .direct("What were the cones used for?", "\"We use them to shape traffic around a lane closure on the road project. We stacked fourteen at the edge of the work zone at dusk for our crew to pick up in the morning.\""), .direct("How can you tell they were yours?", "\"Each cone has the company's name stamped on the base and a number written on it with paint marker. They match the fourteen on our equipment sheet.\""), .direct("How did you find out they were gone?", "\"When I came back at eight the stack was missing. I checked the work zone camera and saw a truck back up and a person loading the cones one at a time.\""), .cross("The cones were stacked for pickup, weren't they?", "\"Yes, they were stacked for our crew to collect. They were not thrown away.\""), .cross("Did {D} hide what {D.he} was doing?", "\"No. {DL} loaded them in the open.\""), .cross("Did the defendant take them anywhere?", "\"The dump, I understand. I do not know more.\""), .cross("The stack was not fenced off or labeled, was it?", "\"It was not fenced, but the cones were stacked neatly by the road with our stamp on the bases. We do not usually put signs on them.\""), .cross("You do not know where they ended up besides what you were told, do you?", "\"I was told the dump. I have not seen them since, and I did not follow up to find out for sure.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took cones.", "Discards."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("The cones had a company stamp.", "They were stacked for pickup."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you take the cones?", "\"Yes, I did. I thought they were trash. They were stacked at the edge of the site.\""), .direct("Why did you take them?", "\"I was cleaning up and I thought the contractor had left them. I did not see a stamp.\""), .direct("Where did you take them?", "\"To the dump. I did not keep them or sell them.\""), .direct("What were you doing near the work zone?", "\"I was clearing debris from a vacant lot next door for a landlord. The cones were stacked in a pile and looked like part of the junk.\""), .direct("Why did you think they were trash?", "\"They were dirty and some had cracks. They were piled at the edge of the lot instead of being set out, so I figured the crew had left them.\""), .direct("How did you load them?", "\"One by one into the bed of my truck, in the open, with headlights on the work zone. I did not hurry because I assumed it was all trash.\""), .cross("The cones have a company stamp. Didn't you see it?", "\"I did not look. I just loaded them.\""), .cross("You loaded fourteen cones at dusk. Why then?", "\"That was when I was clearing things. I did not think it mattered.\""), .cross("Did you ask anyone if they were trash?", "\"No. I wish I had. I made an assumption.\""), .cross("You did not read the company name on the base, did you?", "\"No. I was working in low light and I did not think to look. I own that.\""), .cross("You never asked the crew or the contractor, did you?", "\"No. I assumed it was junk and made a bad call, and I regret not asking.\"")],
        openings: ("Fourteen traffic cones worth $280 were stacked for pickup at a road work zone at dusk. By 8 p.m. they were gone, and the work zone camera shows {D} loading them into a truck.", "Jurors will learn that {D} was clearing debris next to the zone, believed the pile was trash, and took the cones openly to the dump. {D} kept nothing and tried to hide nothing."),
        closings: ("Fourteen stamped cones stacked at the edge of a work zone were loaded into {D}'s truck and carried off. A company stamp on every base told anyone who looked that they were not trash.", "{D} loaded the cones in plain view and took them to the dump, believing they were junk. That is a careless assumption, not an intent to steal."),
        timeline: [(0, "Dusk: the cones are stacked."), (0, "8 p.m.: they are gone.")],
        identified: "Work Zone Camera",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let ebayBrick = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.ebayBrick",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Seller Ships Brick Instead of E-Bike"],
        law: "falsePretenses",
        spec: "Obtained property of {V} by deception, $900, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} took $900 for an e-bike on {DATE} and shipped a brick in the box. The sale was on a Monday and the box arrived on Friday. The listing promised an e-bike.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Shipping Box", "A brick inside."), E(.document, 2, "Listing", "A listing for an e-bike at $900.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Mix-Up", "{DL} says the boxes were swapped.")],
        role: "Buyer",
        exam: [.direct("What did you buy on {DATE}?", "\"An e-bike for $900. The listing promised an e-bike, and I paid on a Monday.\""), .direct("What arrived?", "\"A box on Friday. When I opened it, there was a brick inside. There was no e-bike and no note.\""), .direct("What do the listing and the box show?", "\"The listing was for an e-bike at $900. The shipping box held a brick. I photographed it and kept the box.\""), .direct("How did you find the listing?", "\"I saw it on a resale site on Monday morning, an e-bike with a 500 watt motor for $900, described as lightly used. The seller had decent reviews and photos of the bike in a garage.\""), .direct("How did you pay and what were you told?", "\"I paid $900 through the site's payment link that same day. The seller messaged that it would ship by ground and arrive within the week.\""), .direct("What exactly did you find in the box?", "\"A single red brick wrapped in a plastic grocery bag and surrounded by crumpled newspaper. There was no bike, no charger, and no paperwork inside.\""), .cross("{DL} says the boxes were swapped, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"I can't say who swapped anything. I only know what arrived at my door.\""), .cross("Did you speak with {DL} afterward?", "\"I messaged {D}. I was told it was a mix-up. I never got the e-bike or my money back.\""), .cross("Could the shipper have made a mistake?", "\"It's possible, but a brick isn't a normal mistake. A brick means someone put a brick in the box.\""), .cross("The tracking shows a single box, doesn't it?", "\"Yes, one package with one tracking number, delivered Friday. It matched the label that was shipped to my address.\""), .cross("You did not film yourself opening the box, did you?", "\"I took pictures of the brick and the box right after I opened it, but I did not record the opening. The photos have timestamps.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} shipped a brick.", "A mix-up."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} posted three other listings.", "The tracking shows one box."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you ship {V} a brick?", "\"No. I shipped what I thought was the e-bike. I don't know how a brick got in the box. The boxes must have been swapped.\""), .direct("Why do you think the boxes were swapped?", "\"I had more than one package that day. Something got mixed up at the shipper or in transit. I can't explain it any other way.\""), .direct("Did you try to fix it?", "\"I told {V} I'd look into it. I didn't get far. I should have refunded the money.\""), .direct("How many items were you shipping that week?", "\"I had listed three other items and shipped more than one package on the same day. I was packing quickly in a cramped garage.\""), .direct("What did you do once the buyer wrote to you?", "\"I told {V} I would check my records and the other boxes. I got busy with work and did not follow up the way I know I should have.\""), .direct("What is your process for packing a large item like a bike?", "\"I use a flat bike box with foam and tape the label on top. I did that for this one, I believe, but I cannot swear to what went in which box.\""), .cross("You took $900 for the e-bike, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I received the money. I didn't return it. I know that's a problem.\""), .cross("A brick isn't a box swap, is it?", "\"It's what arrived. I can't explain it. I know it sounds hard to believe.\""), .cross("You never sent {V} an e-bike, did you?", "\"I thought I did. If it didn't arrive, I'm sorry about that, and I will refund the money.\""), .cross("You kept the $900, correct?", "\"I did, and I should have refunded it as soon as the problem came up. I have the money and I owe it back.\""), .cross("You cannot produce a photo of the bike in the box, can you?", "\"No, I do not have one. I did not take a photo of the packed box, and I understand that hurts my account.\"")],
        openings: ("{V} paid $900 for an e-bike on a Monday, and on Friday a box arrived with a brick inside. The listing promised a bike, the box held a brick, and {D} kept the money.", "The defense will point to a seller who was shipping several packages that week and believes boxes were swapped in a rushed garage. {D} meant to send an e-bike and has never claimed otherwise."),
