        law: "larcenyMerchant",
        spec: "Took merchandise valued at $240 from {V}, a clothing store, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} wore store clothes under {D.his} own out of a fitting room on {DATE}. {D} went into the fitting room at 2 p.m. and left at 2:20 p.m. in extra layers. The three tops were worth $240 together.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Store Camera", "{D} walks out in extra layers."), E(.document, 2, "Price Tags", "Three tops priced at $240 in total.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Forgot", "{DL} says {D.he} forgot them.")],
        role: "Store manager",
        exam: [.direct("What did you see on camera on {DATE}?", "\"{D} went into the fitting room at 2 p.m. and came out at 2:20 wearing extra layers. {D.He} walked out of the store like that.\""), .direct("What was the value of what left?", "\"Three tops priced at $240 in total. The price tags are in evidence. {DL} wore them under {DL}'s own clothing.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I reviewed the camera after I found clothes missing from the fitting room count. I reported it to deputies.\""), .direct("How do your fitting rooms work?", "\"Staff hand out a numbered tag and count the items going in. Each customer is supposed to bring out everything they took in, and we count again at the door of the fitting area.\""), .direct("What did the count show for {D}?", "\"{D.He} went in with six items at 2 p.m. and came out at 2:20 with three. The attendant was pulled to the register and did not recount.\""), .direct("What did the footage show after that?", "\"{D.He} walks out of the fitting area, past the registers, and out the front door wearing a bulkier top than when {D.he} went in. You can see the edge of a different collar showing underneath.\""), .cross("{DL} says {D.he} forgot them, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Forgetting three tops under your clothes is hard to picture, but I can't say what {D.he} was thinking.\""), .cross("Did you stop {DL} at the door?", "\"No. I didn't see it live. I only saw it afterward on camera, so no one confronted {D.him}.\""), .cross("Did {DL} try to hide the clothes?", "\"The tops were under {D.his} own clothes. That's a kind of hiding. But I can't say whether it was deliberate.\""), .cross("Tags were not found on the items when you recovered them, were they?", "\"They were not. The tags had been snipped off, though I do not know whether a fitting room lets customers do that.\""), .cross("{D} came back to the store later, didn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes, about a week after. By then we had already opened the case, and {D.he} brought some of the tops back.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} walked out in store clothes.", "Forgetfulness."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} removed the tags.", "{DL} returned later."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why were you wearing the store's tops?", "\"I tried them on and I forgot to take them off. I put my own clothes on over them without thinking.\""), .direct("Did you mean to leave with them?", "\"No. I'd never walk out with something I didn't pay for. I was distracted when I left.\""), .direct("How long were you in the fitting room?", "\"About twenty minutes. I tried on a lot. I got mixed up, and I didn't realize until later.\""), .direct("What did you take into the fitting room?", "\"About six items, a mix of tops and a pair of pants. I was trying to find something for an event and tried most of them on.\""), .direct("What did you do with the clothes you tried on?", "\"I hung up what did not fit and wore the layers I liked out of the room while I looked at a mirror. I got a phone call and walked around talking.\""), .direct("When did you notice the extra tops?", "\"At home that evening I felt the tags poking my back. I was horrified and decided to bring them back on my next day off.\""), .cross("Three tops under your clothes is a lot to forget, isn't it?", "\"Yes. I understand how that sounds. I was layered in that weather, so I didn't feel them.\""), .cross("You walked out of the store wearing them, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. I didn't realize. If I'd known, I'd have gone back.\""), .cross("You didn't pay for any of them, did you?", "\"No. I didn't. I wasn't planning to buy them. I only tried them on.\""), .cross("The tags were cut off, weren't they?", "\"They were, but I do not remember doing it. I was distracted on the phone and may have done it without thinking.\""), .cross("You walked right past the registers without paying, correct?", "\"Yes. I did not think I was carrying anything unpaid, which is the problem with how it looked.\"")],
        openings: ("At 2 p.m. {D} went into a fitting room with six items and at 2:20 walked out of the store wearing three of the store's tops under {D.his} own clothes. The tags were cut off, and the tops were worth $240.", "The defense will present a customer who tried on too many things during a long phone call, lost track, and brought the tops back. {D} never meant to leave without paying."),
        closings: ("Twenty minutes in a fitting room, three tags cut off, and a walk past the registers in extra layers. A person can forget a lot, but not three tops pulled over their own shirt.", "A distracted shopper who realized the mistake at home and returned the clothes is not a thief. The State has not proved {D} meant to steal rather than lost track in a busy fitting room."),
        timeline: [(0, "2 p.m.: the fitting room."), (0, "2:20 p.m.: the exit.")],
        identified: "Store Camera",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .female])

    static let gateArm = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.gateArm",
        category: .traffic,
        headlines: ["Driver Plows Through Parking Gate Arm Without Paying"],
        law: "injuryPersonalProperty",
        spec: "Willfully and wantonly injured personal property of {V}, a parking operator, causing damage of $350, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} drove through a gate arm on {DATE} to avoid a $12 fee. The garage exit is a single lane with a gate arm and a pay station. The exit came at 1 a.m., and the arm snapped a second later.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Gate Camera", "{D} plows through the arm."), E(.document, 2, "Repair Invoice", "$350 to replace the gate arm.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Stuck", "{DL} says the gate stuck.")],
        role: "Garage manager",
        exam: [.direct("What happened at your garage exit at 1 a.m. on {DATE}?", "\"{D} drove up to the single-lane exit and went straight through the gate arm. The arm snapped a second later.\""), .direct("What was {DL} trying to avoid?", "\"A $12 fee at the pay station. The garage charges at the exit, and the gate is supposed to lift after the fee is paid.\""), .direct("What did the damage cost?", "\"$350 to replace the gate arm. The invoice is in evidence. The arm was broken and the lane was shut until we fixed it.\""), .direct("How does a driver leave your garage?", "\"The exit is a single lane with a pay station. The driver inserts a ticket, pays by card or cash, and a gate arm rises for about ten seconds.\""), .direct("What does the camera show about the arm?", "\"It shows {D.his} car pulling up behind another vehicle, waiting, then accelerating as the first car clears. The arm drops onto the hood and snaps off at the hinge.\""), .direct("How did the gate behave for the car before {D}?", "\"It raised normally, held for the usual count, and lowered after the car cleared. The log shows no error code for that cycle.\""), .cross("{DL} says the gate stuck, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"The gate has had issues, but the camera shows the car driving forward into the arm, not stopping at it.\""), .cross("Did the pay station show any problem that night?", "\"Not that I know of. I didn't see any error record. That doesn't mean it can't happen, but I have no log of a fault.\""), .cross("Did {DL} stop and report the damage?", "\"No. {D.He} kept driving. I only learned about it from the camera the next day.\""), .cross("This gate arm has had trouble before, hasn't it?", "\"We had a service call about a sticky arm in the spring. It was repaired, and the maintenance record shows it passed inspection after that.\""), .cross("You cannot see inside the pay station from the camera, can you?", "\"Correct. I can see the car at the machine, but I cannot see what the screen displayed or whether {D.he} had a ticket.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} broke a gate.", "A stuck gate."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had no ticket.", "The gate raised normally for the prior car."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you drive through the gate arm?", "\"The gate was stuck. I tried the pay station and it wouldn't work. It was late, and I was in a hurry, so I drove through.\""), .direct("Did you try to pay the fee?", "\"I tried. The machine didn't respond right. I wasn't trying to avoid the $12. I would have paid it if it had worked.\""), .direct("Why didn't you report the damage?", "\"I was embarrassed and in a hurry. I should have called the garage or left a note. I didn't think about it.\""), .direct("What happened at the pay station?", "\"I could not find my ticket and the machine kept asking me to insert it. I pressed the help button, and nothing happened.\""), .direct("What did you see about the gate?", "\"It stayed down. I waited about a minute, then it looked like it was lifting a little when the car ahead moved, so I eased forward.\""), .direct("Why did you leave without reporting it?", "\"It was one in the morning and I was exhausted. I told myself the gate was at fault and drove home, and that was a mistake.\""), .cross("The camera shows you driving into the arm, doesn't it?", "\"It shows my car going through. I didn't see the arm snap. I just kept going.\""), .cross("$12 isn't much to avoid, is it?", "\"No. That's why I'm telling you I wasn't avoiding it. I'd have paid, but the gate wouldn't open.\""), .cross("It was 1 a.m., wasn't it?", "\"Yes, late at night. I was tired and wanted to get home. I made a poor decision.\""), .cross("You did not have a ticket, did you?", "\"No, I had lost it. I probably owed the lost ticket charge, which is higher than $12.\""), .cross("The arm was down when you drove forward, wasn't it?", "\"It was down or only partly up. I should have waited for the attendant, and I did not.\"")],
        openings: ("At 1 a.m. {D} drove a car through a garage exit gate arm and snapped it, apparently to avoid a $12 fee. The gate camera records the car accelerating, and a new arm cost $350.", "Jurors will hear about a pay station that did not respond, a gate that seemed to lift, and a tired driver who made a poor decision at one in the morning. {D} did not set out to destroy a gate."),
        closings: ("A $12 fee and a $350 gate arm. The camera shows {D} accelerating through at 1 a.m. instead of waiting for help, and the gate worked normally for the car before.", "The gate stuck, the machine failed, and {D} drove forward in a hurry without meaning to break anything. The State has not proved that a tired mistake was a plan to avoid a fee."),
        timeline: [(0, "1 a.m.: the exit."), (0, "1:01 a.m.: the arm snaps.")],
        identified: "Gate Camera",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let wifiBorrow = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.wifiBorrow",
        category: .cyber,
        headlines: ["Man Uses Former Roommate's Wi-Fi After Password Change"],
        law: "accessingComputers",
        spec: "Accessed a computer network of {V} without authority, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} logged into an ex-roommate's network on {DATE} after the password was changed. The password was changed fourteen days before the router log was pulled. The log shows {D}'s phone connecting every night.",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "Router Log", "{D}'s phone appears every night."), E(.document, 2, "Password Change Record", "The router password changed fourteen days before.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Open", "{DL} says it was open.")],
        role: "Homeowner",
        exam: [.direct("What did your router log show?", "\"{D}'s phone connecting to my network every night. It showed up for about two weeks.\""), .direct("When did you change the password?", "\"Fourteen days before I pulled the log. I changed it after {D.he} moved out.\""), .direct("Did {D} have permission to use it?", "\"No. {D.He} was an ex-roommate, and I had changed the password to end access.\""), .direct("How did the defendant come to know your network?", "\"{D.He} was a roommate for about a year and knew the password because we shared it. When {D.he} moved out I changed it to a new phrase.\""), .direct("How did you notice something was wrong?", "\"My internet slowed down at night and I pulled the router's device list. {D.his} phone name showed up every evening around ten.\""), .direct("What did you see in the log across the two weeks?", "\"The phone connected each night for between one and three hours, for fourteen days straight. It was always the same device name and the same hardware address.\""), .cross("Did the old password still work?", "\"The log suggests the old one still worked. I did not know that when I changed it.\""), .cross("Did you tell the defendant not to use it?", "\"I did not tell {D.he} directly. I assumed the password change was enough.\""), .cross("Did the defendant take anything or damage anything?", "\"No. {D.He} only used the connection.\""), .cross("You did not send the defendant a message about the new password, did you?", "\"No. I assumed {DL} would understand that moving out meant giving up access, so I never said it directly.\""), .cross("The old password was still working, correct?", "\"The log suggests it was, because the router did not fully kick off old devices. I did not realize that until I checked.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} used someone's network.", "An open network."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("The password was changed.", "The old password still worked."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you log into the network?", "\"Yes. The old password still worked, so I kept connecting.\""), .direct("Why did you keep using it?", "\"I did not think it was a problem. It still worked, and I did not know I was not allowed.\""), .direct("Did you know the password had changed?", "\"I knew it was supposed to. I did not think it mattered when the old one worked.\""), .direct("Where were you when you connected?", "\"I was parked outside on the street, since my new place had no internet yet. The signal reached the curb, and the phone connected on its own.\""), .direct("What did you use it for?", "\"Mostly streaming shows and checking email for about an hour each night. I did not look at any files or devices on the network.\""), .direct("What would you have done if you had known you were not welcome?", "\"I would have turned the wifi off and paid for my own service sooner. I never wanted to cause any trouble.\""), .cross("You were told to stop, weren't you?", "\"I do not remember being told. If I had been, I would have stopped.\""), .cross("Every night for two weeks. Isn't that deliberate?", "\"I was using it from outside.\""), .cross("You moved out of that home, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I should have understood that I was no longer welcome on the network.\""), .cross("The password was changed after you moved out, correct?", "\"So I understand, yes. I did not check, and the phone just kept reconnecting.\""), .cross("You kept returning every night for two weeks, didn't you?", "\"I did, because it worked. I did not stop to ask myself whether I still had permission.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} kept logging into an ex-roommate's wifi network every night for two weeks after the password was changed. The router log shows {D}'s phone each evening, and the homeowner never gave permission.", "By the end of this trial, the proof will show that the old password still worked, that nobody told {D} to stop, and that {D} touched nothing on the network. A connection that opens by itself is not a break-in."),
        closings: ("The password was changed, and {D}'s phone kept showing up every night for fourteen days. The log is clear, and moving out ends a right to someone's network.", "The old password kept working and nobody told {D} to stop. A device that reconnects by itself for two weeks, used only for streaming, is not the work of someone breaking in."),
        timeline: [(-14, "The password changes."), (0, "The router log.")],
        identified: "Router Log",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let curbCouch = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.curbCouch",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Man Takes Couch From Curb That Was Not Free"],
        law: "misdLarceny",
        spec: "Stole property of {V}, valued at $400, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} loaded a couch from a curb on {DATE} that its owner was waiting to sell. The couch was set out in the morning and was gone by evening. {V} had put a for-sale sign on it.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Doorbell Camera", "{D} and a friend load the couch."), E(.document, 2, "Listing", "The couch listed for $400.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Free", "{DL} says curb items are free.")],
        role: "Owner",
        exam: [.direct("What did you do with your couch on {DATE}?", "\"I set it out at the curb in the morning with a for-sale sign on it. It was listed for $400 and I was waiting for a buyer.\""), .direct("What happened to it?", "\"By evening it was gone. My doorbell camera shows {D} and a friend loading it into a vehicle.\""), .direct("Was there anything on the couch to show it wasn't free?", "\"Yes. I'd put a for-sale sign on it. I listed it for $400, and I wanted to make that clear to anyone who stopped.\""), .direct("How was the couch listed?", "\"I posted it online for $400 with photos and set it by the curb that morning with a hand-lettered sign taped to the back cushion. I told buyers to come after work.\""), .direct("What does your doorbell camera show?", "\"Two people pull up in a pickup around six that evening, look at the couch, lift it together, and load it. They drive off without ringing the bell.\""), .direct("How did you notice it had vanished?", "\"I came out to meet a buyer at seven and the curb was empty. The sign was lying face down on the grass nearby.\""), .cross("{DL} says curb items are free, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"A lot of people think so. But I had a sign on it and a listing, so it was clearly for sale.\""), .cross("Was the sign easy to see?", "\"I put it where I thought it would be seen. I can't say what angle {DL} saw it from. I know it was on the couch.\""), .cross("Did you speak to {DL}?", "\"No. I was inside. I only know what the camera shows. I came out to find the couch gone.\""), .cross("The sign was taped to the back of the couch, wasn't it?", "\"Yes, to the back, facing the street. It may have been blown down, and it may have been face down by the time {DL} came.\""), .cross("You did not post a notice that it was not free, did you?", "\"Only the for-sale sign. I did not think of anything else because I assumed a sign would be enough.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took a couch.", "Curb rules."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("A 'for sale' sign sat on it.", "The sign was face down."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you take the couch?", "\"It was at the curb. I thought it was free for the taking. Lots of people put things out like that, and I figured it was too.\""), .direct("Did you see the sign?", "\"I may have seen something on it. I didn't read it. I thought it was a note about the couch, not a price.\""), .direct("Did you try to hide what you were doing?", "\"No. I loaded it in the evening with a friend, in full view of the street. I wouldn't have done that if I thought it wasn't free.\""), .direct("How did you spot the couch?", "\"I was driving home with a friend and saw it on the curb in front of a house. There was no one around and it looked like it was waiting for trash day.\""), .direct("What did you do with it?", "\"We loaded it into my friend's truck together and took it to my apartment. I gave it a good scrubbing and put it in my living room.\""), .direct("Did you notice the listing or any sign?", "\"There may have been a sign somewhere, but I did not see one. If I had, I would have knocked on the door.\""), .cross("There was a for-sale sign, wasn't there?", "\"I understand there was. I didn't pay attention to it. I should have looked closer.\""), .cross("The couch was listed for $400, wasn't it?", "\"I didn't know that. If I had, I'd have left it.\""), .cross("You and a friend loaded it into a vehicle, didn't you?", "\"Yes. It was heavy. I wasn't sneaking, and I'd have given it back if anyone had asked.\""), .cross("You did not knock on any door, did you?", "\"No, I did not. I assumed that a couch on a curb was free to take, which was an assumption and not a fact.\""), .cross("You have since offered to pay for it, haven't you?", "\"Yes, I offered $400 once I learned the price. I did not want to keep something that was not mine.\"")],
        openings: ("{V} set a couch at the curb with a for-sale sign, listed for $400. By evening, {D} and a friend had loaded it into a truck and driven off, and the doorbell camera recorded it.", "The defense will point to a person who believed a couch at a curb was free, who loaded it in the open, and who never saw a sign. {D} has offered to pay the listing price."),
        closings: ("A couch with a for-sale sign and a $400 listing, and two people loading it away on camera. Taking an item without asking turns a curb into a crime scene only when the person knows it is for sale.", "A couch at a curb looks free to many people, and {D} took it in the open without hiding anything. The sign was face down and the State has not proved {D} knew it was for sale."),
        timeline: [(0, "Morning: the couch is posted."), (0, "Evening: it is gone.")],
        identified: "Doorbell Camera",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let barrelBurn = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.barrelBurn",
        category: .publicOrder,
        headlines: ["Man Burns Trash in Barrel and Refuses to Put It Out"],
        law: "disorderly",
        spec: "Disturbed the peace of {V}, a neighbor, by burning refuse, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} kept burning trash in a barrel on {DATE} after two requests to stop. The smoke began at noon and drifted toward the neighbor's house. The fire marshal visited at 12:30 p.m.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Neighbor Camera", "Smoke from {D}'s yard."), E(.statement, 2, "Fire Marshal", "Saw smoke and a burn barrel in {D}'s yard.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Permit", "{DL} says {D.he} burns yard waste.")],
        role: "Neighbor",
        exam: [.direct("What was going on at {DL}'s house on {DATE}?", "\"{D} was burning trash in a barrel. The smoke began at noon and drifted toward my house. I'd already asked {D.him} twice to stop.\""), .direct("What does your camera show?", "\"Smoke rising from {D.his} yard and blowing across the property line toward my home. It shows the barrel and the smoke.\""), .direct("Who else saw it?", "\"The fire marshal visited at 12:30 and saw the smoke and the burn barrel in {D.his} yard.\""), .direct("What did the smoke look like?", "\"It was thick and dark gray with a sharp chemical smell, not the light white smoke of leaves. It rose from the barrel at the back of {D.his} yard and rolled right into our open windows.\""), .direct("How many times did you ask {D} to stop?", "\"Twice. Once over the fence at about ten that morning and again at noon when the smoke got worse. {D.He} said it was only yard waste both times.\""), .direct("What did the fire marshal do when arriving?", "\"The marshal walked around the barrel, looked inside, and wrote down what was visible. I saw the marshal pull out what looked like melted plastic with a stick.\""), .cross("{DL} says {D.he} burns yard waste, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Some burning of yard waste is allowed. But I'd asked {D.him} to stop twice, and the smoke bothered us.\""), .cross("Did the smoke damage anything?", "\"No. It drifted in, and we had to close windows. No property was damaged, though it was unpleasant.\""), .cross("Did you call the fire marshal?", "\"Yes. I called after the second request didn't work. I didn't want to make a fuss, but the smoke kept coming.\""), .cross("Burning yard waste is allowed in our county in some seasons, isn't it?", "\"It is, with conditions. My complaint is the plastic smell and the fact that we asked twice.\""), .cross("You did not see what went into the barrel, did you?", "\"I saw {DL} drop a couple of bags in from the fence line. I do not know what they held.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} burned trash.", "Yard waste."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("Plastic was in the barrel.", "No permit was posted."),
        defendant: [.direct("What were you burning?", "\"Yard waste, mostly. Leaves and brush. It's what we do around here, and I didn't think it was a problem.\""), .direct("Did your neighbor ask you to stop?", "\"Yes. Twice. I didn't stop because I thought what I was doing was allowed. I should have listened.\""), .direct("What did you do when the fire marshal came?", "\"I stopped and talked to the fire marshal. I put out the barrel when asked. I didn't argue.\""), .direct("What was the barrel used for?", "\"It is an old steel drum I use to burn leaves and brush that pile up each fall. We have always burned out there, and so did the previous owners.\""), .direct("What went in the barrel that day?", "\"Mostly branches and leaves, plus a couple of paper feed bags. I may have tossed in a few small plastic pots as well, and I did not think much of it.\""), .direct("What happened when the marshal arrived?", "\"I put the lid on the barrel and answered every question. I put out the fire and told the marshal I would not burn again until I got clearer rules.\""), .cross("You were asked to stop twice, weren't you?", "\"Yes. I thought it was a minor matter. I wasn't trying to cause problems, but I didn't stop.\""), .cross("The smoke drifted toward your neighbor's house, didn't it?", "\"I've been told that. I didn't notice at the time. I should have paid attention.\""), .cross("You didn't have a permit, did you?", "\"I didn't think I needed one for yard waste. I know now I should have checked.\""), .cross("Your neighbor asked you twice to stop, didn't they?", "\"Yes, and I told them it was only yard waste. I brushed off the second request, and I should have taken it more seriously.\""), .cross("You never posted or pulled a burn permit, did you?", "\"No. I did not think one applied to leaves, and I never called to check.\"")],
        openings: ("After two requests from a neighbor to stop, {D} kept burning trash in a barrel, and smoke rolled toward the neighbor's open windows by noon. The fire marshal arrived at 12:30 and found a burn barrel and the smell of plastic.", "The defense will present a person who has burned leaves in the same barrel for years and who put out the fire and cooperated when the fire marshal came. {D} did not see a permit as necessary for brush."),
        closings: ("Two requests to stop, a barrel still burning, and thick smoke drifting into a neighbor's house. The marshal saw it, and plastic does not belong in a burn barrel.", "{D} burned leaves and brush the way {D.his} household always had and stopped when an official asked. The State has not proved the barrel held more than ordinary yard waste."),
        timeline: [(0, "Noon: the smoke."), (0, "12:30 p.m.: the fire marshal.")],
        identified: "Neighbor Camera",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let paradeRoute = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.paradeRoute",
        category: .publicOrder,
        headlines: ["Man Runs Onto Parade Route and Blocks a Float"],
        law: "disorderly",
        spec: "Disturbed the peace by blocking a public event, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: false,
        summary: "{D} ran in front of a parade float on {DATE} and refused to move. The float came up at 11 a.m., and deputies arrived ten minutes later. The parade ran along the main street.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Street Camera", "{D} stands in front of a float."), E(.statement, 2, "Parade Marshal", "Asked {D} to move several times.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Protest", "{DL} says it was a protest.")],
        role: "Parade marshal",
        exam: [.direct("What happened at the parade?", "\"At about 11 a.m., {D} ran in front of a float and refused to move. The parade ran along the main street.\""), .direct("How many times did you ask {D} to move?", "\"Several. I asked {DL} repeatedly to step aside, and {DL} refused.\""), .direct("What did the defendant have with {D.him}?", "\"A sign. {D.He} stood in the road holding it. There was no permit for a protest.\""), .direct("How is the parade organized?", "\"We run it along the main street each year with a permit from the town. Floats line up at the high school and head downtown, and marshals walk alongside at every block.\""), .direct("What did the defendant do exactly?", "\"{D.He} stepped off the curb at the corner of Main and Third, raised a hand-lettered sign, and stood in front of a float carrying the high school band. The float stopped.\""), .direct("What did you tell the defendant?", "\"I walked up and said we had a permit and asked {D.him} to return to the sidewalk. I asked four more times over the next several minutes.\""), .cross("Did the defendant touch the float or anyone on it?", "\"No. {D.He} just stood there. There was no violence.\""), .cross("How long was the float stopped?", "\"About ten minutes, until deputies arrived. Then {D.he} was moved.\""), .cross("Were you in danger?", "\"No. The float was moving slowly. But it could have hurt someone.\""), .cross("{D} never touched the float, did {D.he}?", "\"No, {D.he} stood about six feet in front of it. The driver stopped in time, and nobody was touched.\""), .cross("Deputies arrived within ten minutes, correct?", "\"Yes, around 11:10. They asked {DL} to move, and {DL} did after a short exchange.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} stopped a parade.", "A protest."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had a sign.", "No permit for a protest."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you block the parade float?", "\"Yes, I did. I stood in front of it on purpose, because I wanted to protest and be seen.\""), .direct("What were you protesting?", "\"A cause I care about deeply. I wanted people along the route to see my sign and think about it.\""), .direct("Did you carry a sign?", "\"Yes, I did. I carried a sign the whole time, and I stood peacefully without touching anything.\""), .direct("What was on your sign?", "\"It named a cause I care deeply about and asked drivers and the crowd to take it seriously. I made it the night before with poster board.\""), .direct("Why did you choose a parade?", "\"It was where the largest crowd would be, and I had tried emails and letters before with no response. I thought people would listen if I stood in the road.\""), .direct("How did you feel when deputies came?", "\"Nervous, but I walked to the curb with them without a struggle. I knew I had delayed a parade full of families and I felt bad about it.\""), .cross("You refused to move when the marshal asked, didn't you?", "\"I did. I wanted to be heard, and I did not want to give up my spot in the road.\""), .cross("You did not have a permit for a protest, did you?", "\"No. I did not know that I needed one, and nobody ever told me before the parade.\""), .cross("The parade was delayed ten minutes. Isn't that disruptive?", "\"It was, and I understand that. I accept the consequences of what I chose to do.\""), .cross("The marshal asked you to move several times, correct?", "\"Four or five times, I believe. I heard each request and I chose to stay, and I will not say otherwise.\""), .cross("You did not apply for any protest permit, did you?", "\"No, I did not. I did not know the process, and I should have asked before I acted.\"")],
        openings: ("At 11 a.m., {D} stepped off the curb in front of a parade float on the main street and refused to move despite repeated requests from the parade marshal. Deputies arrived ten minutes later, and the parade stood still until then.", "Jurors will see a peaceful protester holding a sign who harmed no one. {D} stood in the road for a cause {D} cares about, and the float was never touched."),
        closings: ("A parade with a permit, a float, and {D} standing in the road after four or five requests to move. A parade ran for the whole town, and a right to protest does not include stopping it.", "{D} held a sign and stood peacefully. No one was touched or threatened, and a protest that delayed a parade for ten minutes is a poor reason to criminalize a speaker."),
        timeline: [(0, "11 a.m.: the float."), (0, "11:10 a.m.: deputies arrive.")],
        identified: "Street Camera",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let weddingCrasher = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.weddingCrasher",
        category: .publicOrder,
        headlines: ["Uninvited Man Crashes Private Wedding and Refuses to Leave"],
        law: "trespass2",
        spec: "Entered and remained on the premises of {V}, a private venue, after being notified not to, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} joined a wedding reception on {DATE} and ignored two requests to leave. Dinner began at 6 p.m., and deputies arrived at 6:40 p.m. The venue is a private hall.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Venue Camera", "{D} fills a plate and sits."), E(.document, 2, "Guest List", "{D}'s name is not on the list.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Invited", "{DL} says a guest invited {D.him}.")],
        role: "Venue manager",
        exam: [.direct("How did {D} come to be at the reception?", "\"{D} walked into our private hall during a wedding reception. Dinner began at 6, and {D.he} filled a plate and sat down.\""), .direct("Was the defendant on the guest list?", "\"No. {DL}'s name is not on the list. The venue camera shows {DL} entering and eating.\""), .direct("How many times was the defendant asked to leave?", "\"Twice. {D.He} stayed, and deputies arrived at about 6:40.\""), .direct("How is a wedding reception checked in at your venue?", "\"The couple gives us a guest list and place cards. A host at the door checks names against it, though once dinner begins the door is often left open for caterers.\""), .direct("What did the camera show about the defendant?", "\"{D.He} walks in the side door at about 5:50, picks up a plate at the buffet, and sits at an empty seat near the back. {D.He} eats and talks with nobody.\""), .direct("What happened when you approached the defendant?", "\"I asked if {D.he} was with the party, and {D.he} said a guest had invited {D.him}. I asked who, and {D.he} could not give a name, so I asked {D.him} to leave.\""), .cross("Did a guest wave {D} in?", "\"I understand one guest did. I did not see that myself.\""), .cross("Did the defendant cause any disturbance?", "\"No. {D.He} sat quietly and ate. There was no fight.\""), .cross("Did any guest recognize the defendant?", "\"None that I know of. No guest knew {D.him} as far as I learned.\""), .cross("The side door was open at that time, wasn't it?", "\"Yes, the caterers were bringing in trays. It is something we need to tighten up.\""), .cross("{D} took only one plate of food, correct?", "\"I saw one plate, and a second small one with cake. Nothing else was taken.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} crashed a wedding.", "A guest's invite."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("No guest knew {DL}.", "One guest waved {DL} in."),
        defendant: [.direct("Were you invited to the wedding?", "\"I thought I was. A guest waved me in as I walked by, and I assumed that meant I was welcome.\""), .direct("Why did you refuse to leave when asked?", "\"I wanted to finish eating first. I was embarrassed and did not want to make a scene in front of everyone.\""), .direct("Did you know the couple getting married?", "\"No, I did not know them at all. I never met them, and I did not claim to.\""), .direct("How did you end up at the venue?", "\"I was walking by and saw lights and music through the side door. A guest in a suit waved me in as I stood outside, so I walked in.\""), .direct("Why did you eat at the table?", "\"I was hungry and thought I had been invited. I took a seat near the back and kept quiet so I would not bother anyone.\""), .direct("Why did you stay after being asked to leave?", "\"I was embarrassed and wanted to finish the plate before going. I also did not want a scene in front of the couple.\""), .cross("You were not on the guest list, were you?", "\"No, I was not. I did not check, and I thought the wave from a guest was enough.\""), .cross("You were asked twice to leave, weren't you?", "\"Yes, I was. I should have left right away, and I am sorry that I did not.\""), .cross("You filled a plate at a wedding you were not invited to, didn't you?", "\"Yes, I did. It was a bad choice, and I am embarrassed about it.\""), .cross("You did not know the couple, did you?", "\"No, not at all. I never saw their names until I looked at the place cards on the table.\""), .cross("You could not name the guest who waved you in, could you?", "\"No. It was a quick wave from a stranger, and I did not ask any names.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} walked into a private wedding reception, filled a plate, and sat down. {D} was not on the guest list, was asked twice to leave, and stayed until deputies arrived at 6:40 p.m.", "The defense case is that a guest waved {D} in, that {D} caused no trouble, and that {D} was slow to leave out of embarrassment. A hungry passerby is no threat to a wedding."),
        closings: ("A private reception, a guest list without {D}'s name, and two requests to leave that went unanswered. Dinner began at 6 p.m. and deputies had to arrive at 6:40 to end it.", "A wave from a stranger, a plate of food, and no trouble at all. {D} should have left sooner, but the State has not proved more than a hungry person's poor judgment."),
        timeline: [(0, "6 p.m.: dinner."), (0, "6:40 p.m.: deputies arrive.")],
        identified: "Venue Camera",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let scooterHome = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.scooterHome",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Rider Takes Rental E-Scooter Home Instead of Returning It"],
        law: "misdLarceny",
        spec: "Stole property of {V}, a scooter company, valued at $650, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} kept a rental scooter at home for a week on {DATE}. The rental began seven days before the agent found the scooter at {D}'s home. The app logged the scooter parked there for the week.",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "App Record", "The scooter parked at {D}'s home for a week."), E(.document, 2, "Rental Terms", "A rental ends when the ride is ended in the app.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Forgot", "{DL} says {D.he} forgot to end the ride.")],
        role: "Company agent",
        exam: [.direct("How did you find the scooter?", "\"Seven days after the rental began, I found our scooter parked at {D}'s home. The app had logged it sitting there for the whole week.\""), .direct("How does a rental normally end?", "\"By ending the ride in the app. The rental terms say the rental ends only when the rider ends the ride, and until then the meter runs.\""), .direct("Did the company try to reach {D}?", "\"Yes. The app sent alerts every day for the week. I do not have a record of {DL} replying to any of them.\""), .direct("How does the company track its scooters?", "\"Every scooter has a GPS unit and reports to our app each few minutes. The map shows whether a rental is active, parked, or idle, and the system flags any scooter that sits still for more than a day.\""), .direct("What did the app show for this scooter?", "\"It showed the rental starting on a Monday evening and then the scooter sitting at one residential address for seven days. The battery level dropped each day until it hit zero.\""), .direct("What alerts went out to the renter?", "\"The app sent a push notification each morning saying the ride was still active and the meter was running. We also sent an email on day three and a text on day five.\""), .cross("The scooter was parked, not in use, correct?", "\"It sat parked at {D.his} home all week. The log shows no riding, and I will agree it was not being used.\""), .cross("Was the battery dead when you found it?", "\"Yes, the battery was dead. That may be why it was not moving, but it was still on {D.his} property.\""), .cross("Did the defendant resist when you came to collect it?", "\"No. {D.He} handed it over without any trouble. {D.He} did not hide it.\""), .cross("The scooter was not damaged when you recovered it, was it?", "\"No. It had a few scuffs but nothing beyond normal wear. The battery was dead because it had sat unused all week.\""), .cross("{D} was charged for the full week of rental time, correct?", "\"The app charged the daily cap for each day, which came to a few hundred dollars. That may have been what {D.he} meant to dispute.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} kept a scooter.", "Forgetfulness."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("The app sent alerts daily.", "The battery was dead."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you keep the rental scooter at your home?", "\"Yes, I did. I rode it home one evening, parked it, and then never ended the ride in the app.\""), .direct("What about the alerts from the company?", "\"I ignored them. I thought they were just reminders, and I did not look closely at what they said.\""), .direct("Did you ever end the ride in the app?", "\"No. I forgot. I was busy, and I assumed leaving it parked would stop the charges.\""), .direct("What happened on the evening you rented it?", "\"I rode it home from a friend's place because the buses had stopped running. I parked it by my front door and meant to end the ride before bed.\""), .direct("Why did you not end the ride?", "\"I got a work call as I walked in and forgot all about it. I saw the app icon but did not think of the meter running.\""), .direct("What did you think when the company agent knocked?", "\"I was shocked that a week had passed and said so right away. I wheeled it out, handed it over, and apologized.\""), .cross("Seven days of alerts and you never opened one, did you?", "\"I saw some of them. I should have read them, but I did not take them seriously.\""), .cross("The scooter was in your home for a week. Didn't you know it belonged to someone else?", "\"Of course I knew it was a rental. I just did not think it through, and I regret that.\""), .cross("You did not return it until the company came to you, did you?", "\"That is right. I did not return it myself. I am sorry for the trouble.\""), .cross("Daily alerts went out, didn't they?", "\"I saw a few on my lock screen and swiped them away. I assumed they were ads and I should have read them.\""), .cross("You could have taken it back in an hour, couldn't you?", "\"Yes. A short walk would have fixed it, and I did not do that.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} rented a scooter, parked it at home, and never ended the ride. Seven days later a company agent found it there with a dead battery, after the app had sent daily alerts.", "Jurors will learn that {D} forgot to end the ride in the app, believed the alerts were advertisements, and handed the scooter back without argument. Forgetting an app is not the same as keeping something."),
        closings: ("A rental scooter sat at {D}'s home for a full week while the app sent an alert every day. {D} knew it belonged to the company and never returned it.", "This was a forgotten tap on a phone, not a plan to keep a scooter. The battery died, the alerts looked like ads, and {D} gave it up the moment someone came."),
        timeline: [(-7, "The rental."), (0, "The agent finds it.")],
        identified: "App Record",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let casinoChips = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.casinoChips",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Man Cashes Fake Chips at Casino Cage"],
        law: "falsePretenses",
        spec: "Obtained property of {V}, a casino, by deception, $400, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} tried to cash fake chips at a casino cage on {DATE}. {D} reached the cage at about 9 p.m., and security stopped {D} ten minutes later. The chips weighed less than genuine ones.",
        state: [E(.physical, 3, "Chips", "Chips with the wrong weight."), E(.statement, 2, "Casino Cashier", "The chips failed the weight check.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Won", "{DL} says {D.he} won them.")],
        role: "Casino cashier",
        exam: [.direct("What happened at your cage window at about 9 p.m. on {DATE}?", "\"{D} came to the cage to cash some chips. I ran them through the weight check, and they failed.\""), .direct("What was wrong with the chips?", "\"They weighed less than genuine chips. That's one of the ways we catch fakes. A real chip has a known weight.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I called security. They stopped {DL} about ten minutes later. I kept the chips for evidence.\""), .direct("What does your weight check involve?", "\"We set each chip on a calibrated scale and compare it to the standard weight for its denomination. Genuine chips of this kind are within a fraction of a gram, and these were noticeably lighter.\""), .direct("How many chips did {D} bring to you?", "\"A stack of twelve in the hundred dollar color, worth $1,200 on the face. They looked right at first glance, with the right edge spots and the casino's logo.\""), .direct("Who stopped the defendant and when?", "\"A security officer walked up about ten minutes after I made the call. {D.He} was standing at the window and went along calmly.\""), .cross("{DL} says {D.he} won the chips, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"I can't say where they came from. I only know the chips failed the weight check.\""), .cross("Did {DL} try to run?", "\"No. {D.He} stayed at the window and waited. {D.He} was calm and polite.\""), .cross("Are all fake chips obvious?", "\"No. A good fake can pass at a glance. That's why we check weight. I can't tell by looking.\""), .cross("{D} did not leave the window while you waited, did {D.he}?", "\"No. {D.He} stayed put and chatted about the night. I did not see any sign of trying to leave.\""), .cross("You did not see where those chips came from, did you?", "\"No. I was at the cage, not on the floor. A pit boss might have seen the table, and I cannot say who played where.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} passed fake chips.", "A winner."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("The chips were counterfeit.", "A pit boss saw {D.him} win."),
        defendant: [.direct("Where did you get those chips?", "\"I won them at a table. I played for a while and cashed in what I had. I didn't know they were fake.\""), .direct("Why did you take them to the cage?", "\"To cash out. I'd had a good night. I wanted to go home with my winnings.\""), .direct("What did you do when security came?", "\"I stayed and answered questions. I'd never try to cash fake chips. I was stunned.\""), .direct("What were you playing that night?", "\"I sat at a blackjack table for about three hours. I started with a couple hundred dollars and had a good run in the last hour.\""), .direct("How did you receive the chips?", "\"The dealer pushed them to me when I won a few hands in a row. I stacked them in front of me, and I did not count them closely.\""), .direct("Why did you go to the cage?", "\"It was getting late and I was ahead, so I decided to cash out and head home. I carried the stack straight across the floor.\""), .cross("The chips failed the weight check, didn't they?", "\"That's what the cashier says. I don't know why. I never weighed them.\""), .cross("You can't say who gave you the chips, can you?", "\"I played at a table with a dealer. I don't remember details. I thought they were real.\""), .cross("You walked straight to the cage, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I was going to cash out. I didn't hide anything.\""), .cross("You do not know why the chips were light, do you?", "\"I really do not. I never touched a scale, and I trusted what the dealer paid me.\""), .cross("You cannot point to the dealer by name, can you?", "\"No. I did not catch a name and I could not tell you which one was working. I would have remembered a face.\"")],
        openings: ("At about 9 p.m. {D} reached a casino cage with a stack of chips that failed the weight check, and security stopped {D} ten minutes later. The chips were lighter than genuine ones and counterfeit.", "The defense will present a gambler who says the chips were won at a table, who walked straight to the cage in the open, and who stood and waited. A person trying to pass fakes does not stay at the window."),
        closings: ("Chips that weigh less than genuine chips, presented at the cage by {D}. The scale does not lie, and the stack was not real.", "{D} won chips at a table and went to cash them in the open. The State has not proved {D} knew they were fake, and a pit boss's account fits with a night of winning."),
        timeline: [(0, "9 p.m.: the cage."), (0, "9:10 p.m.: security.")],
        identified: "Chips",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let offeringPlate = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.offeringPlate",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Man Takes Cash From Church Offering Plate After Service"],
        law: "misdLarceny",
        spec: "Stole property of {V}, a church, valued at $300, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} pocketed an offering plate's cash on {DATE} after a service. The plate went around at noon, and the count came up short at 12:30 p.m. The plate held about $300.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Sanctuary Camera", "{D} pockets cash."), E(.document, 2, "Count Sheet", "The counters' sheet shows a short count.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Counting", "{DL} says {D.he} was helping count.")],
        role: "Church usher",
        exam: [.direct("What happened with the offering plate after the service?", "\"The plate went around at noon and held about $300. When the counters finished at 12:30, the count came up short.\""), .direct("What does the sanctuary camera show?", "\"It shows {D} pocketing cash from the plate after the service, when the plate was set down. It is a short clip, but it is clear.\""), .direct("How do your counters usually handle the plate?", "\"Counters sign a count sheet. Two people are assigned, and the sheet is the record of what was counted.\""), .direct("How does the plate go around during a service?", "\"Two ushers pass baskets down each pew while the choir sings. The ushers carry them to a side room afterward and set them on a table for counting.\""), .direct("Who counts the offering?", "\"Two assigned counters, usually a deacon and a volunteer, count it in the side room and sign a sheet. We have done it that way for years so that no one is left alone with cash.\""), .direct("What did the camera show you?", "\"{DL} stands at the table in the sanctuary after the service, takes a handful of bills from the plate, and slides them into a jacket pocket. Then {DL} leaves by the main doors.\""), .cross("{D} says {D.he} was helping count, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"That is what {D.he} says. But {D.he} was not one of the counters, and no sheet bears {D.his} name.\""), .cross("Did anyone ask the defendant to help with the count?", "\"I do not believe so. I did not, and I have not heard of anyone who did.\""), .cross("How much exactly was missing?", "\"I cannot give you a certain figure. The count was short, and I would be guessing at the exact amount.\""), .cross("The counters' sheet showed a short count, correct?", "\"Yes. The tally came to a few dollars less than the plate's usual take, and we estimated the plate held about $300.\""), .cross("You cannot say how much the defendant actually took, can you?", "\"I cannot give an exact figure from the camera. I know bills went into a pocket, but the count is only an estimate.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took offerings.", "Helping count."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("Counters sign a sheet.", "{DL} signed no sheet."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you take cash from the offering plate?", "\"I was helping count the money. I picked up some bills to count them, and I put them in my pocket while I did.\""), .direct("Did you sign a count sheet?", "\"No. There was no sheet for me to sign. I was only helping on my own.\""), .direct("Who asked you to help count?", "\"Nobody. I saw the plate sitting there and thought I would help out, and I did not think about permission.\""), .direct("What were you doing at the table?", "\"I saw the plate sitting alone after the last hymn and thought I would help gather it. I picked up a handful of bills to carry to the side room.\""), .direct("Why did you put the money in your pocket?", "\"My hands were full of my coat and Bible. I stuck the bills in my pocket to carry them, with the plan to put them on the table as I walked in.\""), .direct("What happened next?", "\"A friend stopped me in the lobby and we talked for twenty minutes. By the time I reached the side room, the counters had gone.\""), .cross("Counters sign a sheet. You did not, did you?", "\"No. I was not one of the counters, and I should have asked before touching the money.\""), .cross("You put the money in your pocket instead of on the table, didn't you?", "\"I did, and I realize how that looks. I was holding it while I sorted.\""), .cross("The count came up short after you left. How do you explain that?", "\"I cannot explain it. I did not keep any of the money, and I am sorry that it looks otherwise.\""), .cross("You did not hand the money to a counter, did you?", "\"No. I never made it back to the room, and that is what I regret.\""), .cross("You were not one of the assigned counters, correct?", "\"Right. Nobody asked me to help, and I acted on my own.\"")],
        openings: ("After a service, the offering plate held about $300. A sanctuary camera shows {D} putting a handful of bills from it into a pocket and walking out, and the counters' sheet came up short.", "The defense evidence will establish that {D} was trying to help carry the money, never signed a sheet, and got caught up in a conversation in the lobby. {D} had no plan to keep a dollar."),
        closings: ("The camera shows {D} putting cash from the offering plate into a pocket, and the count came up short thirty minutes later. Nobody had asked {D} to handle it.", "{D} meant to help and made a clumsy choice about where to put the bills. The State has not proved a taking rather than a muddled attempt at being useful."),
        timeline: [(0, "Noon: the plate."), (0, "12:30 p.m.: short.")],
        identified: "Sanctuary Camera",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let fakeDealerTag = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.fakeDealerTag",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Man Makes and Mounts Fake Dealer Plate"],
        law: "forgery",
        spec: "Forged a dealer license plate of the State of North Carolina, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: false,
        summary: "{D} made a fake dealer plate and drove with it on {DATE}. The stop came at noon, and the plate was seen ten minutes later. The plate was a painted copy of a dealer tag.",
        state: [E(.physical, 3, "Fake Plate", "Painted plate with no state mark."), E(.document, 2, "Plate Photo", "A photo of the painted plate on the car.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Prop", "{DL} says it was a prop.")],
        role: "Deputy",
        exam: [.direct("What did you see at noon on {DATE}?", "\"I stopped a car with a dealer-style plate. About ten minutes later, I took a closer look at it and noticed something was off.\""), .direct("What was wrong with the plate?", "\"It was a painted copy of a dealer tag with no state mark. It was hand-painted, not an official plate.\""), .direct("What did you do with it?", "\"I photographed the plate on the car and took the plate as evidence. The photo and the plate itself are in evidence.\""), .direct("What made you stop the car?", "\"I was running a routine patrol at noon and saw a dealer-style plate on a sedan that did not look like a dealer vehicle. The paint was a bit uneven and the letters were wide.\""), .direct("What did you notice up close?", "\"The plate lacked the state seal and the stamped border of a real tag. It was made of thin painted metal and the characters were hand lettered.\""), .direct("What did {D} tell you?", "\"{D} said it was a prop made for a car show and that the car was for sale. {DL} handed me a driver's license and registration without argument.\""), .cross("{DL} says it was a prop, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"A prop on a public road isn't a prop anymore. It was on the car and driven.\""), .cross("Did {DL} try to deceive you?", "\"I don't think {D.he} tried to hide it. The plate was in plain view. {D.He} was cooperative.\""), .cross("Could it have been mistaken for a real plate?", "\"From a distance, yes. A painted plate can fool a casual glance. Up close, it clearly wasn't official.\""), .cross("The car had a proper registration, didn't it?", "\"The registration was valid, and the actual tag was in the back window. The dealer plate was attached on the front only.\""), .cross("{D} was cooperative, wasn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. {D.He} answered everything I asked and did not try to explain it away.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} forged a plate.", "A prop."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("The car was for sale.", "A buyer was texting."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why was a painted plate on your car?", "\"It was a prop. I'd made it for a project, and I mounted it for fun. I didn't think anyone would take it seriously.\""), .direct("Did you mean to deceive anyone?", "\"No. I didn't intend to fool anyone. I thought it looked like a joke. I know now that was a bad idea.\""), .direct("What did you do when the deputy stopped you?", "\"I told the deputy it was a prop. I handed over the paperwork I had. I wasn't hiding anything.\""), .direct("How did you make the plate?", "\"I bought a blank aluminum tag at a craft store and painted the border and letters with stencils. I did it over a weekend in the garage.\""), .direct("Why did you put it on the car?", "\"I was selling the car and wanted it to look like a dealer lot piece in photos. I mounted it on the front to take pictures and forgot to take it off before driving.\""), .direct("How long had it been on the car?", "\"About two days. I drove to the store and back and then to the gas station, and that is when the deputy stopped me.\""), .cross("It was painted by you, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I painted it. It looked pretty good. That's probably why it was a problem.\""), .cross("There was no state mark on it, correct?", "\"Right. I knew it wasn't real. I should not have put it on a car I drove.\""), .cross("You drove on a public road with it, didn't you?", "\"Yes, and I know a prop should stay in the driveway. I did not take it seriously.\""), .cross("You knew it would look real to others, didn't you?", "\"From a distance, perhaps, which is why I made it for photos. I did not mean it to fool a deputy.\""), .cross("You were driving on a public road with a plate that was not a state-issued tag, weren't you?", "\"Yes. I used it to show the car was for sale and I forgot it was still on. I understand why a deputy would stop that car.\"")],
        openings: ("A deputy stopped a car at noon and found a painted copy of a dealer plate with no state mark. {D} made the plate, mounted it, and drove on a public road with it.", "The defense evidence includes a car listed for sale, a prop plate mounted for photos, and a driver who was open with the deputy. {D} never tried to pass it off as a state tag."),
        closings: ("A hand-painted dealer plate with no state mark, on a car on a public road. {D} made it, and a plate that can fool a glance is a plate someone can be fooled by.", "{D} made a prop, said so right away, and had real tags and registration in order. The State has not proved {D} meant to pass it off as genuine."),
        timeline: [(0, "Noon: the stop."), (0, "12:10 p.m.: the plate is seen.")],
        identified: "Fake Plate",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let pharmacyPills = SmallCases.make(
