        headlines: ["Man Throws City Bike-Share Bike Into River"],
        law: "injuryPersonalProperty",
        spec: "Willfully and wantonly injured personal property of {V}, a city, causing damage of $1,100, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} threw a bike-share bike off a bridge on {DATE}. The bike went over the rail at 11 p.m. and was recovered the next day. The city's recovery and replacement came to $1,100.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Bridge Camera", "{D} lifts the bike over the rail."), E(.document, 2, "Recovery Invoice", "$1,100 to recover and replace the bike.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Dare", "{DL} says it was a dare.")],
        role: "City bike manager",
        exam: [.direct("What happened to your bike-share bike on {DATE}?", "\"A bike went over a bridge rail at 11 p.m. It was recovered from the water the next day, and the city's cost came to $1,100.\""), .direct("What does the bridge camera show?", "\"It shows {D} lifting the bike over the rail. You can see the bike go over and {D.he} watching it fall.\""), .direct("What does the $1,100 cover?", "\"Recovering the bike and replacing it. We had to hire a crew and replace the bike because it wasn't usable.\""), .direct("How does the bike-share system work?", "\"Riders unlock a bike with the app, ride it, and park it at a dock or in a designated zone. Each bike has a tracker and a lock that reports its status to us.\""), .direct("How did you recover this bike?", "\"We got a missing-bike report the next morning, found the last tracker ping at the bridge, and sent a diver and a tow crew. We pulled it out of the river that afternoon.\""), .direct("What was the condition of the bike?", "\"The frame was bent, the battery housing cracked, and the wheel was twisted. It was a total loss, and the $1,100 covers the recovery crew and a new bike.\""), .cross("{DL} says it was a dare, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"I can't speak to whose idea it was. The camera shows {DL} lifting it.\""), .cross("Was anyone hurt?", "\"No. It went into the water. Nobody was below, as far as we know. It could have been dangerous.\""), .cross("Could the bike have been damaged earlier?", "\"It was in working condition when last checked. I can't say what happened after that.\""), .cross("The bike was working when last used, wasn't it?", "\"Yes, the previous rider logged a normal trip an hour earlier and nothing was reported wrong.\""), .cross("You did not see who pushed it over except on the camera, correct?", "\"Correct. I was not there. I rely on the bridge footage, which shows {DL} and a few others.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} drowned a bike.", "A dare."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("The bike was reported missing.", "{DL} filmed it."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you throw the bike off the bridge?", "\"It was a dare. Friends said I wouldn't do it. It was a dumb thing to do, and I did it.\""), .direct("Did you think about the cost?", "\"No. I didn't think it would matter. I thought it was a joke. I know that's no excuse.\""), .direct("How do you feel about it now?", "\"I would say I feel foolish. I'd undo it if I could.\""), .direct("Who was with you that night?", "\"Two friends who were filming on their phones. One said I would never do it, and I wanted to prove I would.\""), .direct("What exactly did you do?", "\"I walked the bike to the rail, lifted the front end, and tipped it over. It fell about thirty feet into the water.\""), .direct("What happened afterward?", "\"We laughed for a moment, then I felt sick when I saw how far it dropped. I left and told no one.\""), .cross("You lifted the bike over the rail, didn't you?", "\"Yes. The camera shows it.\""), .cross("It was a city bike, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I knew it wasn't mine. That makes it worse.\""), .cross("You could have said no to the dare, couldn't you?", "\"Yes. I could have. I wanted to look tough. That was stupid.\""), .cross("Nobody forced you to do it, did they?", "\"No. I could have turned and walked away, and I chose to impress people.\""), .cross("Your friend filmed the throw, didn't they?", "\"Yes. I know the video exists, and it is not a flattering record of that night.\"")],
        openings: ("At 11 p.m. a bridge camera caught {D} lifting a city bike-share bike over a rail and dropping it into the river. The bike was recovered the next day, and recovery and replacement cost $1,100.", "The defense evidence includes a foolish dare from friends who filmed it, a person who accepts fault, and no thought for the cost. {D} acted to impress people and regrets it."),
        closings: ("A city bike over a bridge rail, on camera, and $1,100 to recover and replace it. {D} chose to do it, and a dare does not make the bike any less public property.", "A dare, a thoughtless moment, and an offer to pay. The State has not proved {D} meant more than a stupid stunt that {D} deeply regrets."),
        timeline: [(0, "11 p.m.: the bridge."), (0, "Next day: recovered.")],
        identified: "Bridge Camera",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let neighborTree = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.neighborTree",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Neighbor Cuts Down Tree Over Property Line"],
        law: "injuryRealProperty",
        spec: "Willfully and wantonly injured real property of {V}, causing damage of $1,500, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} cut down a neighbor's oak on {DATE}, claiming it sat on {D.his} lot. The saw started in the morning, and the tree was down by noon. The oak was valued at $1,500.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Survey", "The oak stood on {V}'s side."), E(.document, 2, "Arborist Appraisal", "The oak appraised at $1,500.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Line", "{DL} says the line is disputed.")],
        role: "Neighbor",
        exam: [.direct("What happened to your oak tree?", "\"{D} started a saw in the morning, and by noon my oak was down. It stood on my side of the line.\""), .direct("How do you know it was on your side?", "\"A survey puts the oak on my lot. I have the survey, and it shows the line running behind the tree.\""), .direct("What was the tree worth?", "\"An arborist appraised it at $1,500. It was a mature oak and shaded half my yard.\""), .direct("How old was the oak and where did it stand?", "\"It was about sixty years old and stood near the back corner of my lot, close to the fence. It shaded my patio all afternoon and was the biggest tree on the block.\""), .direct("What did you hear that morning?", "\"A chainsaw started around eight a.m. next door. I walked out and saw {D.him} on a ladder cutting limbs off my oak.\""), .direct("What did you say to {D}?", "\"I shouted across the fence that the tree was mine and asked {D.him} to stop. {D.He} waved me off and kept sawing, and the trunk was down by noon.\""), .cross("{D} says the tree was on {D.his} lot, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. {D.He} believes it was. But the survey says otherwise.\""), .cross("How old is the survey?", "\"It is two years old. I know that may matter, and the line has not moved.\""), .cross("Has {D} ever ordered a new survey?", "\"I do not believe so. I have not heard of one.\""), .cross("The survey on file is two years old, isn't it?", "\"Yes, I had it done when I put up the fence. I know the property pins do not move, but I have not paid for a new one.\""), .cross("The oak's trunk is near the line, isn't it?", "\"It is close to the line, within a few feet. That is why I had the survey done in the first place.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} cut a neighbor's tree.", "A line dispute."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("The survey is two years old.", "{DL} had never ordered a new one."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you cut down the oak?", "\"Yes, I did. I believed it stood on my lot, and I thought I had the right to remove it.\""), .direct("Why did you think it was yours?", "\"My own survey, from years ago, put the line on the other side of the tree.\""), .direct("When was your survey done?", "\"Years ago, before I bought the house. I trusted it, and I never had it redone.\""), .direct("What made you think the oak was on your lot?", "\"My own survey from the closing years ago showed the line running behind the tree. I walked the fence and the oak looked to be on my side.\""), .direct("Why did you decide to cut it?", "\"One big limb hung over my roof and dropped branches every storm. I got a quote for trimming and decided to take the whole tree down myself.\""), .direct("How did you react when your neighbor complained?", "\"I kept cutting for a few minutes because I was sure of my line. After a while I stopped and saw that the survey had to be wrong or I had misread it.\""), .cross("The newer survey puts the tree on {V}'s side, doesn't it?", "\"It does. I did not know about that when I cut. I saw only mine.\""), .cross("You never ordered a new survey, did you?", "\"No. I should have before cutting anything. That was my mistake.\""), .cross("A $1,500 oak is gone. What do you say to {V}?", "\"I truly am sorry. I thought it was mine. I would like to make it right.\""), .cross("You never asked your neighbor where the line ran, did you?", "\"No. I assumed I knew, and I did not want to start an argument over a limb.\""), .cross("A new survey would have cost a few hundred dollars, wouldn't it?", "\"Yes. That is far less than a $1,500 tree, and I regret not spending it.\"")],
