        summary: "{D} changed a former roommate's mail forwarding on {DATE} and kept three packages. The forwarding form was filed on a Monday, and the first package went missing by Friday. The three packages were worth $380.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Forwarding Form", "Filed from {D}'s email address."), E(.document, 2, "Package Records", "Three packages shipped to the old address.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Mistake", "{DL} says it was a clerical error.")],
        role: "Roommate",
        exam: [.direct("What did you notice about your mail?", "\"Three packages shipped to my old address were missing. The first went missing by Friday. They were worth $380 together.\""), .direct("What did you learn about the forwarding?", "\"A forwarding form was filed on a Monday from {D}'s email address. {D.He} is my former roommate.\""), .direct("What do the package records show?", "\"Three packages were shipped to the old address. They show up as delivered, but I never received them.\""), .direct("How did you learn your packages were missing?", "\"I got tracking notices that three packages had been delivered to my old address. When I asked the new tenants they said nothing had come.\""), .direct("How did you trace the forwarding?", "\"I called the post office and was told a change-of-address had been filed on a Monday and sent mail to another address. The filing email was {DL}'s.\""), .direct("What were in the packages?", "\"A pair of boots, a kitchen mixer I bought as a gift, and a set of supplements. Together they came to about $380.\""), .cross("{DL} says it was a clerical error, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"I can't speak to what {D.he} meant. I only know the form was filed in my name and the packages didn't reach me.\""), .cross("Were you living at the old address?", "\"No. I'd moved out. That's why my mail was still going there. I should have updated it earlier.\""), .cross("Did you ask {DL} about the packages?", "\"Yes. {D.He} said it was a mistake. I never got the packages back.\""), .cross("The form was signed, wasn't it?", "\"It carried a signature that looked like mine, but I never signed it. I do not know whether {D.he} signed it or typed my name.\""), .cross("One of the packages came back, didn't it?", "\"Yes, the mixer was returned a few weeks later with a note. The boots and the supplements were never returned.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} redirected packages.", "A mistake."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("The form was signed by {DL}.", "One package was returned."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you file a forwarding form?", "\"I was trying to forward my own mail and mixed up the names. It was a clerical error. I didn't mean to take anything.\""), .direct("What happened to the packages?", "\"They came to my address because of the form. I opened them without thinking. I didn't realize they were my former roommate's.\""), .direct("Did you intend to keep them?", "\"No. I would have given them back. I wasn't paying attention, and I know I should have.\""), .direct("What were you trying to do with the form?", "\"I had moved from the same building and meant to forward my own mail. I filled out the form quickly and put my former roommate's name in the wrong box.\""), .direct("When did you notice the packages?", "\"They started showing up at my door that week, addressed to my roommate. I stacked them in my closet and told myself I would sort it out.\""), .direct("What did you do with them?", "\"I returned the mixer after a few weeks when I felt guilty. I opened one of the others by mistake and ended up using the supplements.\""), .cross("The form was filed from your email, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I did file it. I made a mistake about whose mail it was.\""), .cross("You kept three packages, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I should have returned them as soon as I knew. I didn't, and I regret it a lot.\""), .cross("Your former roommate wasn't forwarding anything to you, was {V.he}?", "\"No. I just filed the form. I should have checked the name. It was my fault.\""), .cross("You never contacted your former roommate about the packages, did you?", "\"No. I should have texted the same day and I did not, because I was embarrassed.\""), .cross("One of the packages was returned, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I sent one back after I realized the mix-up. I should have sent all three and told my old roommate what had happened.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} filed a mail forwarding form on a Monday in a former roommate's name, and by Friday the first of three packages worth $380 had gone missing. The form came from {D}'s own email address.", "The defense will present a clerical error, a form filed in the wrong box, and a person who returned one package when conscience caught up. {D} never meant to take what belonged to a roommate."),
        closings: ("A forwarding form from {D}'s email, three packages gone, and $380 lost. A mistake that lasts for weeks and costs a roommate three packages is not a harmless clerical error.", "A clerical mix-up is not a plan to steal. {D} filed the form under {D.his} own email, returned one package, and never hid where the mail went."),
        timeline: [(0, "Monday: the form."), (0, "Friday: the first package.")],
        identified: "Forwarding Form",
