        role: "Cardholder",
        exam: [.direct("What happened to your wallet on {DATE}?", "\"I lost it in the morning. By evening, my cards had been swiped. $120 in cash was gone from the wallet too.\""), .direct("What do the card records show?", "\"$300 in charges that evening. The store camera shows {D} swiping the cards.\""), .direct("What was the total loss?", "\"$420, which is the $120 in cash and the $300 in charges. I had to cancel the cards and report everything.\""), .direct("How did you lose your wallet?", "\"It slipped out of my jacket while I was loading groceries into my car at about nine that morning. I did not notice until I reached for my keys at lunch.\""), .direct("What was in the wallet?", "\"My driver's license, two bank cards, a credit card, and $120 in cash in twenties. My home address was printed on the license.\""), .direct("What did you do when you noticed it was gone?", "\"I retraced my steps to the store lot and checked with the manager. Then I called my bank, but by evening the cards had already been used.\""), .cross("{DL} says {D.he} meant to return the wallet, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"But the cards were used that evening. That doesn't fit with returning it.\""), .cross("Could {DL} have found the wallet and not known whose it was?", "\"The wallet had my cards and ID. I'd think that would tell someone who it belonged to.\""), .cross("Did {DL} contact you at any point?", "\"No. I never heard from {D.him}. I only found out when I saw the charges.\""), .cross("You did not hear from {D} after you lost it, correct?", "\"No call, no mail, and nothing left at the store. My address was on the license, so I would have expected a knock.\""), .cross("The charges were all on one evening, weren't they?", "\"Yes, three swipes at the same store between six and seven o'clock. They came to $300.\"")],
