        truths: ("{DL} used the cards three times.", "The wallet had an address."),
        defendant: [.direct("How did you come across the wallet?", "\"I found it on the ground. I picked it up and planned to return it. I put it in my pocket.\""), .direct("Did you use the cards?", "\"Yes. I did. I was in a bad place and I told myself I'd pay it back. I know that was wrong.\""), .direct("Why didn't you return the wallet?", "\"I kept putting it off. I spent some of the cash and used the cards. I made a series of bad choices.\""), .direct("Where did you find the wallet?", "\"On the pavement near a bus stop at about ten that morning. I opened it to see whose it was and found a driver's license and the cash.\""), .direct("What did you tell yourself?", "\"That I would mail it back that week with the license inside. I put it in my jacket and went on with my day.\""), .direct("Why did you use the cards?", "\"I was behind on rent and groceries, and I convinced myself I would pay it back. I swiped the cards three times at the grocery store that evening.\""), .cross("You took $120 from the wallet, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I took it. I'm ashamed. I didn't have money, and I let myself justify it.\""), .cross("The store camera shows you swiping the cards, doesn't it?", "\"Yes. That's me. I used them for things I needed, and I shouldn't have.\""), .cross("You said you meant to return it, didn't you?", "\"I did mean to at first. Then I didn't. I apologize.\""), .cross("You took the cash first, didn't you?", "\"Yes, the $120 went into my own pocket before I even left the bus stop. I told myself I would return the rest.\""), .cross("You never mailed the wallet back, did you?", "\"No. I kept putting it off, and then I was too ashamed to send it.\"")],
