        truths: ("{DL} kept taking deposits after the notice.", "The notice is real."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you keep taking deposits?", "\"I hoped to reopen. I thought I could find a new space and keep my bookings.\""), .direct("Did you plan to refund the deposits?", "\"Yes. I always intended to refund them if I could not reopen. I never meant to keep the money.\""), .direct("Did you tell customers about the eviction notice?", "\"No. I did not tell them. I was embarrassed and hoped it would work out.\""), .direct("What happened to the shop's lease?", "\"My landlord gave me an eviction notice after I fell behind on rent. I thought I could get a new location lined up within a few weeks.\""), .direct("Why did you keep booking customers?", "\"Because I believed I would reopen. I took deposits on the schedule I planned to keep and put the money toward moving costs.\""), .direct("What happened to the deposits?", "\"They went to rent arrears and a deposit on a new space that fell through. I did not have the cash to refund anyone when the doors closed.\""), .cross("You kept taking deposits after the notice, didn't you?", "\"I did. I know I should have stopped. I did not want to turn people away.\""), .cross("You did not warn anyone that the shop might close, did you?", "\"No. That was a mistake. I should have been honest.\""), .cross("You went dark without telling customers, didn't you?", "\"The shop closed fast. I was overwhelmed and I did not reach everyone.\""), .cross("You did not tell customers about the notice, did you?", "\"No. I told myself it would blow over and I was afraid they would cancel.\""), .cross("The money was spent on your own bills, wasn't it?", "\"Yes, on shop bills I owed. I am working out refunds for each person.\"")],
