        role: "Homeowner",
        exam: [.direct("What did you find in your backyard on {DATE}?", "\"The coop was empty by dawn. I'd counted six hens the evening before, worth about $150. They were gone.\""), .direct("What does your yard camera show?", "\"It shows {D} carrying a crate. It shows the gate being opened at night and {D.he} walking toward the coop.\""), .direct("How do you know the hens were there?", "\"I fed them the evening before. I counted six, and the coop was fine. In the morning, there were none.\""), .direct("What kind of hens did you keep?", "\"Six hens, a mix of brown layers and two speckled ones, in a coop my family built. They laid about four eggs a day, and we had them for two years.\""), .direct("How is the coop secured?", "\"A wire gate latches with a hook, and I check it every evening. I counted all six and latched it around eight that night.\""), .direct("What did you see the next morning?", "\"The gate was open, the coop was empty, and a few feathers lay in the grass. I checked the camera and saw {DL} come in carrying a crate.\""), .cross("{DL} says the hens were loose, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"They were in the coop when I last saw them. I don't know how they'd be loose.\""), .cross("Could the hens have escaped on their own?", "\"It's possible if a gate was left open. But the camera shows {DL} with a crate, which doesn't fit stray hens.\""), .cross("You did not see the hens leave, did you?", "\"No, I was asleep. I only know the coop was empty and my camera shows what it shows.\""), .cross("Hens could roam if a gate was open, couldn't they?", "\"They could, but they roost at night and do not go far in the dark. I never found one wandering.\""), .cross("The coop gate was latched when you went to bed, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I latched it every night, so I do not think the hens got out on their own, but I did not see them leave.\"")],
